00:00:00.177 --> 00:00:01.071
- This one's (bleep) good.

00:00:01.071 --> 00:00:04.640
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.129
I'm excited to have some Macca's.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:06.902
- Bam.

00:00:06.902 --> 00:00:11.168
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:12.612
This sort of looks like
a breakfast burger.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.770
- OK.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.439
- It's a basic burger.

00:00:14.439 --> 00:00:15.822
- It's pretty standard McDonald's.

00:00:15.822 --> 00:00:17.243
- I feel like this is
a burger that I'd maybe

00:00:17.243 --> 00:00:18.970
keep in my pocket and save it for later.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.844
- Bacon's a bit different.

00:00:19.844 --> 00:00:21.205
- This is not bacon.

00:00:21.205 --> 00:00:22.180
This is ham.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.785
- Nothing's like American bacon.

00:00:23.785 --> 00:00:25.878
I mean, you want the thin slices.

00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:26.976
You know, the thick's good,

00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:28.438
but it's like Canadian style.

00:00:28.438 --> 00:00:29.887
- I just can't get around it.

00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:31.444
- Sorry, but I don't think this is bacon.

00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:36.444
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:38.393
It's a nice fancy bun.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:40.181
- Like an everything bagel.

00:00:40.181 --> 00:00:41.156
- It's a pretty big burger.

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:43.107
- There seems to be a lot
of ketchup oozing out.

00:00:43.107 --> 00:00:45.356
- A painting of ketchup on here.

00:00:46.926 --> 00:00:47.881
- Mmmm.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.572
- That's pretty good.

00:00:48.572 --> 00:00:50.705
- The meat to bun ratio
on this is on point.

00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:52.087
- There's actually a lot going on here.

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:53.916
- The sauce was very surprising tasting.

00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:56.009
It kind of just like spurted
out the Mighty Angus.

00:00:56.009 --> 00:01:00.030
- It's more barbecue-y, and hearty,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.712
and like nothing they
would have in the US.

00:01:02.712 --> 00:01:04.785
- It sort of tastes like a cheese steak.

00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:06.044
- The condiments and onions

00:01:06.044 --> 00:01:07.710
are giving me a little
bit of a meatloaf vibe.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.417
- This is the meal you want at three am

00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:10.698
when all the bars close.

00:01:10.698 --> 00:01:12.689
- Definitely not what I remember
from being six years old

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:13.542
and getting a Big Mac.

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:18.500
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.084
- It looks kind of like a Big Mac,

00:01:20.084 --> 00:01:21.465
but a lot smaller.

00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:22.400
- Lots of toppings.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.781
- Looks pretty good.

00:01:23.781 --> 00:01:26.037
- The amount of vegetables
on this is commendable.

00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:28.190
- Almost like your dollar
menu American burger.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.450
- It's like a quarter pounder with mayo.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.096
- So if Big Mac had a little cousin,

00:01:31.096 --> 00:01:31.969
this would be it.

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:34.590
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.484
- Maybe it was just a dream,

00:01:35.484 --> 00:01:38.145
but I feel at one time they
had frozen Coke in the US.

00:01:38.145 --> 00:01:38.923
- Here we go.

00:01:39.893 --> 00:01:41.185
- Woah.

00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:41.986
It's chunky.

00:01:41.986 --> 00:01:43.875
- It doesn't taste like
the Coke I'm used to.

00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:46.131
- Frozen Coke definitely
is better than normal Coke

00:01:46.131 --> 00:01:47.958
'cause then you don't even
have to worry about the ice.

00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:49.889
You don't have to worry about
it watering down your drink.

00:01:49.889 --> 00:01:51.839
- And I wish they had
frozen Coke in the US

00:01:51.839 --> 00:01:54.175
'cause then I could sneak it
into the movie theater with me.

00:01:54.175 --> 00:01:59.175
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:02:00.595 --> 00:02:01.794
- I'm actually from the southwest.

00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:04.496
And when you hand a
Texan a southwest burger,

00:02:04.496 --> 00:02:06.108
it better be legitimate.

00:02:06.108 --> 00:02:09.095
- Stacking it nice and high
with all those toppings.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.838
- When the hell did
McDonald's get so fancy?

00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:12.467
- Oh.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.605
- It's got some like Big Mac sauce.

00:02:13.605 --> 00:02:14.215
What is that?

00:02:14.215 --> 00:02:15.738
- Almost like Taco Bell sauce.

00:02:15.738 --> 00:02:17.384
- Tastes like a collaboration
between McDonald's

00:02:17.384 --> 00:02:18.319
and Taco Bell.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:18.950
- What?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.761
- Nacho chips?

00:02:19.761 --> 00:02:21.183
- Is that a corn chip?

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:23.134
- The chips just add a
really weird texture,

00:02:23.134 --> 00:02:24.150
like it's almost dangerous.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.003
- I'm into it.

00:02:25.003 --> 00:02:26.364
- I think the southwest
is almost like this

00:02:26.364 --> 00:02:28.985
Cajun spicy like herbs that go on it.

00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:30.062
- I mean, it's good flavor.

00:02:30.062 --> 00:02:31.362
Don't get me wrong, it's a good burger,

00:02:31.362 --> 00:02:32.581
but I don't think it has anything to do

00:02:32.581 --> 00:02:33.577
with the southwest.

00:02:33.577 --> 00:02:34.552
- This one's (bleep) good.

00:02:34.552 --> 00:02:35.263
I like this one.

00:02:35.263 --> 00:02:40.263
("Amor Do Reggae")

00:02:41.419 --> 00:02:43.132
- Macca's is just a cool name.

